From: mashen11 <mashen11@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] audio: aidl: default: preserve explicit built-in mic ALSA address in XsdcConversion

createAudioDevice() unconditionally overwrote the XML address of
AUDIO_DEVICE_IN_BUILTIN_MIC with "bottom" or "back", discarding any explicit
ALSA card/device suffix such as "bottom CARD_0_DEV_3" in
primary_audio_policy_configuration.xml and causing StreamPrimary to fall back
to hw:0,0 (which is playback-only on SC8280XP Audioreach topologies).

Only apply the default "bottom" address when the policy configuration leaves
the built-in microphone address empty.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/audio/aidl/default/XsdcConversion.cpp b/audio/aidl/default/XsdcConversion.cpp
index 1a5f7f3c9d..2c7cceced5 100644
--- a/audio/aidl/default/XsdcConversion.cpp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/XsdcConversion.cpp
@@ -236,9 +236,18 @@ ConversionResult<AudioDevice> createAudioDevice(
                                ? AudioDeviceAddress::make<AudioDeviceAddress::Tag::id>(
                                          xDevicePort.getAddress())
                                : AudioDeviceAddress{}};
-    if (device.type.type == AudioDeviceType::IN_MICROPHONE && device.type.connection.empty()) {
+    // Only fall back to the legacy platform default when the audio policy configuration does
+    // not specify an address. Overwriting an explicit address unconditionally makes it
+    // impossible for a device to route its built-in microphone to a dedicated ALSA PCM, because
+    // the address carries the "CARD_<n>_DEV_<m>" selector consumed by
+    // StreamPrimary::getCardAndDeviceId(). When it is lost the primary stream silently falls
+    // back to the default card/device, which on some platforms has no capture PCM at all, so
+    // capture fails to open.
+    const bool addressSpecified = xDevicePort.hasAddress() && !xDevicePort.getAddress().empty();
+    if (!addressSpecified && device.type.type == AudioDeviceType::IN_MICROPHONE &&
+            device.type.connection.empty()) {
         device.address = "bottom";
-    } else if (device.type.type == AudioDeviceType::IN_MICROPHONE_BACK &&
+    } else if (!addressSpecified && device.type.type == AudioDeviceType::IN_MICROPHONE_BACK &&
                device.type.connection.empty()) {
         device.address = "back";
     }
